  "answer": "Project Zenith is a multi-phase initiative focused on data analytics, AI algorithms, and cloud storage optimization. It was introduced in Q3 2023 with a kickoff in June/July, led initially by Sarah Tan and later Marcus Cole, with team expansions including Mike Chen and Lisa Ray. The project received a $2M budget approval, with specific allocations for compliance ($55k) and phase one ($500k). Key milestones include initial findings showing a 20% efficiency increase, a breakthrough in predictive analytics, and a transition from design to development under lead developer Omar Jensen. Updates and reports are shared via meetings scheduled for August 5th, August 1st, and November 20th."
